From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:49:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Estimate the light from grey samples

The white balance followed every coloured area of the scene: a green
cloth turned a white wall blue. The statistics now also sum, apart, the
samples whose colour lies near the white line of the sensor, neither too
dark nor near saturation. With the new greyDistance tuning key the white
balance uses them when they are at least 1% of the samples.

---
Base-commit: 3becb16c1fa22d79a4d7eeb75a36fc895b4b7abf
Source: https://github.com/alessandro-fontana/android_external_libcamera/commit/95f6b20d917be23759710c1f85a6f2deab106e0a

